>> title: Thai Yellow Curry Paste
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: thai, turmeric, paste, chiles, curry
>> counters: Thai Kitchen
>> aka: prik gaeng karee, gaeng karee paste, kaeng kari paste, yellow curry paste, gang garee paste, nam prik gaeng karee
>> pairs-with: thai-yellow-curry, madras-curry-powder
>> servings: 8
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the turmeric goes in raw: toasted it turns muddy, and the yellow is the name of the paste
>> step.1: soak 20 min, drain and chop
>> step.2: toast 2 min, grind in a mortar
>> step.3: pound to a fibrous paste
>> step.4: pound in
>> step.5: work in

Soak @dried long red chiles{6}(stemmed and seeded) in hot water for ~soak{20%min}, then drain and chop them.

Toast @coriander seeds{1%Tbs}, @cumin seeds{2%tsp} and @white peppercorns{1/2%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat for ~toast{2%min}, then grind them to a powder in a #mortar{}.

Pound @&(~2)soaked chiles{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @lemongrass{2%stalks}(tender parts only, thinly sliced), @fresh turmeric{2%Tbs}(peeled and sliced; or 2 tsp dried) and @galangal{1%Tbs}(peeled and chopped) to a fibrous paste.

Pound @garlic{6%cloves} and @shallots{3}(chopped) into @&(~1)paste{}.

Work @&(~3)ground spices{}, @madras curry powder{1%Tbs} and @shrimp paste{2%tsp}(kapi) into @&(~1)paste{} until it is even and the colour of a marigold.
